Reflection depth should be a property of the floor, not of the head standing on it.
Hand-off from the soccer-engine lane to whoever owns play.css. Apply with:

    git apply docs/superpowers/patches/2026-08-11-play-css-reflection-depth.patch

WHY. The falloff mask is written in percentages of the .hmRefl element, and that element
is HH tall, so every head shows the same FRACTION of its own height. Measured at 1440 with
a normal head and mini-Jayden in one frame: element heights 129.6px and 194.4px (ratio
1.500, exactly his size ratio), drawn depths 77.6px and 117.5px, depth/HH 0.599 vs 0.605 --
identical fractions, 1.5x the depth. That is why more of his reflection shows.

It is the wrong law. The fade is the water giving out, and there is one waterline: the feet
plane every head shares. A head being 1.5x taller does not make the water 1.5x clearer, so
the image should die at the same depth below that one line for everybody. play-engine.js
already sets --refl-k on each .hmRefl (1 for a normal head, 0.6667 for the 1.5x mini-Jayden);
this patch is the half that consumes it.

SAFE BY CONSTRUCTION. Every stop is calc(N% * var(--refl-k,1)) and the rule declares
--refl-k:1, so a head with the property unset renders byte-for-byte what it renders today.
Only mini-Jayden moves. Both the water mask and the lobby (body.pHubOn) mask are covered,
including the @supports ripple variant, so the pitch and the polished floor stay consistent.

VERIFY AFTER APPLYING: mini-Jayden's drawn reflection depth should land at ~77.6px, matching
a normal head, instead of 117.5px -- and depth/HH should then differ between them (0.40 vs
0.60), which is the point: shared depth, not shared fraction.
